    {
      "field_name": "other_symptoms_established",
      "value": "myoclonus; dysautonomia; cognitive impairment; inattention; minimal verbal output",
      "quote": "myoclonic jerks and dysautonomia. He required intubation due to subsegmental pulmonary embolism, and propofol and dexmedetomidine were necessary to control violent myoclonic jerks, sympathetic storming, and agitation. Ultimately, he required tracheostomy and gastrostomy tube. His myoclonus, rigidity, and dysautonomia resolved. However, he remained cognitively impaired with inattention and minimal verbal output.",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
